  "notes": "Divine Mill trio under Kay Gee: Chicago-step-flavoured R&B over a sampled bassline, 1997–2002. The research is unusually specific about the groove — \"~100 straight-four (backbeat 2&4) — explicitly 'non-hip-hop-derived straight fours'\" — so the band is narrow at 96–104, `halfTime` is false and, uniquely in this section, `swing.amount` is 0.50 with `offGridMs` 0 and a high quantize strength: the entry says \"no swing\" and \"deliberately *not* boom-bap\" in as many words. The three drum deltas follow: the kick takes real downbeat anchors on 1 and 3 with `fourOnFloorInChorus` true (the entry's house/step-derived chorus kick, marked `[LOW-CONF]`), the snare sits dead flat with almost no ghost activity, and the hats run continuous 16ths at a 0.62 fill density with the open hat on both offbeats — the busiest hat lane in this batch. Harmony is \"diatonic major with a 4-bar cycle\", so the families are functional major and the sourced key is G major, the outlier habit the entry names in a minor-dominated lane. The identifying parameter is the bass: \"the sampled bassline from Kurtis Blow's 'Christmas Rappin'' carries the part — a walking funk line, not a sub\", so `followRootsProb` drops to 0.5, the passing-tone set is the widest here and the cell shapes walk. ⚠ The band is INFERRED around a single point: the entry gives \"BPM ~100 straight-four\" and no band, so the 96–104 cushion is this author's and only the mode, 100, is the entry's own reading. ⚠ The other INFERRED parameters are every velocity and density number and the countermelody; the research gives groove character, key, tempo and the sample, not a kit. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `G`, and the remaining values `C`, `D`, `F`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
